//! Silica C ABI — embedding the engine from C and C-family hosts.
//!
//! An opaque `silica_world*` handle plus functions mirroring the Rust
//! surface of `SPEC.md` §9, with failures reported through a
//! `silica_error` enum and the header generated by cbindgen. The host owns
//! the world handle; there are no callbacks.
//!
//! `unsafe` is allowed in this crate only inside FFI boundary shims, each
//! carrying a `// SAFETY:` comment stating the invariant (AGENTS.md rule
//! 5). None exists yet.
//!
//! Scaffold only — the ABI lands with milestone 0.5 (ROADMAP.md).
